@startuml forms-vol03-fhir
hide circle
hide empty members
skinparam linetype ortho
title Volume 3 - one FHIR pattern for the whole diagnostic catalogue

class ServiceRequest #E6F4EA
class Specimen [[https://dhp.uz/fhir/core/en/StructureDefinition-uz-core-specimen.html{UZ Core Specimen}]] #E8F0FE
class Observation [[https://dhp.uz/fhir/core/en/StructureDefinition-uz-core-observation.html{UZ Core Observation}]] #E8F0FE
class DiagnosticReport
class ImagingStudy
class Encounter [[https://dhp.uz/fhir/core/en/StructureDefinition-uz-core-encounter.html{UZ Core Encounter}]] #E8F0FE

Encounter "1" <-- "0..*" ServiceRequest : « encounter »
ServiceRequest "1" <-- "0..*" Specimen : « request »
Specimen "0..1" <-- "0..*" Observation : « specimen »
Observation "0..*" --> "1" DiagnosticReport : « result »
DiagnosticReport "0..*" --> "0..1" ServiceRequest : « basedOn »
DiagnosticReport "0..1" --> "0..1" ImagingStudy : « study »

note as N
  Almost every form in this volume is an instance of this pattern.

  A "tahlili" (lab analysis: 040-130) is a DiagnosticReport with one
  Observation per result row, linked to a Specimen.

  A "bayoni" / "protokoli" (report: 012, 015-x, 016-026) is a
  DiagnosticReport; imaging adds an ImagingStudy.

  The 015 ultrasound family is one parent (015) plus 26 organ-specific
  children (015-1..015-26) - all the same DiagnosticReport shape.

  A registration "jurnal" (034, 059) is a query over these, not a document.
end note
@enduml
